          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فرش (farsh) is a loan from Arabic farsh, \"anything spread, a carpet\", which reached Urdu through Persian. Its Arabic root is f-r-sh (Lane). In Urdu it came to mean \"the floor\"."
            }
          ]
        },
